{
   "_collider_colours": "In the Scene view every collider is outlined: green solid, cyan trigger, grey disabled, and red while it is touching something (only while playing - nothing has been tested when the clock is paused). The Gizmos menu in the Scene view toolbar switches the whole Colliders category off.",
   "_comment": "THE PHYSICS PLAYGROUND. Thirteen stations on a 4-wide grid, each one exercising a different part of the 2D physics. Open docs/physics-playground.md for what every station is for and what a FAILURE looks like at each one. Select a station root in the Hierarchy to jump to it; press F to frame it.",
   "_keys": "Play, then: E resets the whole playground, SPACE re-launches every body that has a PhysicsLauncher on it. The readout in the top left is the PhysicsLab script on the root entity.",
   "_layers": "Collision layers used here: World (all the static scenery), Default (the dynamic bodies), Trigger, Marker (the reference line in station 4 - it collides with nothing), and PassA/PassB/StopA/StopB for the layer test in station 8.",
